Z||000000||JasonS||02-07-2001||08:33 AM||||I've got an '84 4-cyl 4-speed that runs fairly well...that is until i hammer down the gas pedal.  The engine will sit there and shake until I let up some on the gas and then it kicks in just fine.  Any ideas to fix this aggravation would be greatly appreciated.  It's driveable, but I don't have the passing power that I need.  thanks,<BR>Jason||||reg||8
Z||000001||FieroJoe||02-07-2001||10:15 AM||||Welcome to the Forum!<P>Has the car had a normal tune up lately?  It sounds to me like you have some sort of restriction in your fuel pressure.  Replace the fuel filter if it has not been in a while.  Otherwise, new plugs, wires, air filter, distributor cap/rotor, all part of a regular tune up, should probably solve your troubles.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||02-07-2001||10:21 AM||||When the clutch is in can you rev the engine? It could be the TPS sensor is bad and not sensing a Wide Open Throttle condition. It's located on the side of the throttle body. Do you get a "check engine" light? Another thing that can cause a simular condition is a clogged catalytic converter. Finally a fuel delivery problem. How is the fuel pressure? When was the last time the fuel filter was changed? Does the spray pattern out of the injector look good?<P>That's all I can think of to look at right now.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||JasonS||02-07-2001||11:14 AM||||Thanks for the great suggestions.  I do get a check engine light one the engine warms up to regular temp.  I'm not sure if it's related to that or not.  I'll check to see if I can rev the engine with the clutch in or not.  I have not done a full tune up to it yet, i have just dealt with it.  I have replaced the fuel and air filter and it looks like the guy i bought it from replaced the plugs and wires. I'll check my distributor too.  Thanks again for the help, <BR>Jason||||reg||10
